> solve x = x for x
  ucas: solve x = x for x
solve x = x for x
  x does not occur in the equation
  note: a coefficient is a rounded decimal (numbers in expressions are doubles), so the solutions are approximate
  no real solution
> solve x = 1, x = 2 for x
  ucas: solve x = 1, x = 2 for x
solve x = 1, x = 2 for x
  no solution: the equations are inconsistent (rank 1, the augmented system has rank 2)
> solve 0/0 = x for x
  ucas: solve 0/0 = x for x
solve 0/0 = x for x
  x = real(0/0)
  check: x = it substituted, the equation holds at 0 sample points of the other variables (residual 0)
> solve x^2 + 1 = 0 for x
  ucas: solve x^2 + 1 = 0 for x
solve x^2 + 1 = 0 for x
  note: a coefficient is a rounded decimal (numbers in expressions are doubles), so the solutions are approximate
  no real solution
  (and 2 complex solutions)
